What is MCP (Model Context Protocol)?
MCP is a framework that allows LLMs (like ChatGPT) to interact with external tools (APIs, databases, file systems). Instead of only generating text, the model can:

Call tools
- Retrieve data
- Perform actions

How LLMs use tools
1. User gives prompt
2. LLM decides a tool is needed
3. LLM sends structured request (tool call)
4. Tool executes
5. Output returned to LLM
6. LLM responds to user

